# Roving Actuator: "Void - When this creature enters, if a nonland permanent left the battlefield this turn or a spell was warped
# this turn, exile up to one target instant or sorcery card with mana value 2 or less from your graveyard. Copy it. You may cast the
# copy without paying its mana cost." Turn 1 Bot1 casts Anger of the Gods (mana value 3, just past the limit) into the graveyard;
# Bot2 casts Dark Ritual on turn 2 (mana value 1, but in the other graveyard). On turn 3 Bot1 casts Lightning Helix (mana value
# exactly 2) at Bot2, then sacrifices Black Lotus (a nonland permanent leaving: void) for the Actuator's mana. The trigger refuses
# the Anger and Bot2's Ritual, takes the Helix, exiles it, copies it and casts the copy for free: 3 more damage to Bot2 and 3 more life
# for Bot1. The Ritual stays in Bot2's graveyard, the Anger in Bot1's.

